ffsubsync is used as an installed dependency, not vendored. No upstream source
files are modified or redistributed in this repository. The alignment engine is
invoked through its public Python entry point (ffsubsync.ffsubsync.make_parser
and .run) and its documented CLI flags.

Behavioural claims in README.md about ffsubsync 0.5.1 (ignored --min-score,
success retval on silent reference, cue loss on framerate mis-detection) were
measured against the released package and are reproducible with the fixtures in
fixtures/.
